# {{ .Name }} ({{ .Type }})

> **Requires Portainer Business Edition 3.1 or later.** On Community Edition or an older server the read fails with an error that says so.

**Portainer Business Edition 3.1.0 serves the OIDC provider only when started with the `oidc` feature flag**: `--feat=oidc` (or the environment variable `FEATURE_FLAG=oidc`; Helm chart: `--set "feature.flags[0]=--feat=oidc"`). Without it every OIDC API call fails with an error that says so.

Reads Portainer's launcher (`GET /oidc_launcher`): the enabled OIDC clients with `show_in_launcher` that the user the provider is authenticated as may sign in to. It shows what that user sees, so it is mostly useful to check access from a non-administrator account.

## Example Usage

```hcl
data "portainer_oidc_launcher" "this" {}

output "launcher_links" {
  value = { for e in data.portainer_oidc_launcher.this.entries : e.name => e.homepage_url }
}
```

{{ .SchemaMarkdown | trimspace }}

## Attributes Reference

### `entries`

| Name | Type | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| `name` | string | Name of the client. |
| `description` | string | Description of the client. |
| `homepage_url` | string | URL the launcher opens. |
